/* book exam traps: Do not treat an NTC thermistor as linear. A straight line through two temperatures gives large errors in between. | The ADC count uses full scale 1023 for 10 bits, not 1024. A 5 V reference gives count = round(1023 × V / 5). | TPS redundancy is not two identical signals. The tracks often have opposite slopes or a fixed ratio; the ECU checks agreement, not equality. | A bad sensor ground or 5 V reference shifts TPS and temperature readings together. Check supply and ground before replacing the sensor. | Idle and WOT switches are not analog angle sensors. They only confirm endpoints and cannot replace the TPS curve. */
